{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        new Main().run();\n    }\n\n    void run() {\n        InputReader in = new InputReader(System.in);\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        Solver solver = new Solver();\n        solver.solve(1, in, out);\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    static class Solver {\n        static final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n        static final long INF = (long)1e18 + 1;\n        long[][] nCr = new long[100][100];\n\n        long comb(long base, int a, int b, int c, int d) {\n            base = (base * nCr[a][b]) % MOD;\n            base = (base * nCr[c][d]) % MOD;\n            return base;\n        }\n\n        void solve(int testNum, InputReader in, PrintWriter out) {\n            int n = in.nextInt();\n            int K = in.nextInt();\n            int cnt50 = 0, cnt100 = 0;\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                if (in.nextInt() == 50) cnt50++;\n                else cnt100++;\n            }\n\n            // Precompute binomial coefficients\n            for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) {\n                for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {\n                    if (j == 0 || j == i) nCr[i][j] = 1;\n                    else nCr[i][j] = (nCr[i-1][j] + nCr[i-1][j-1]) % MOD;\n                }\n            }\n\n            long[][][] dist = new long[200][200][2];\n            long[][][] ways = new long[200][200][2];\n            for (int i = 0; i < 200; i++) {\n                for (int j = 0; j < 200; j++) {\n                    Arrays.fill(dist[i][j], INF);\n                    Arrays.fill(ways[i][j], 0);\n                }\n            }\n\n            dist[0][0][0] = 0;\n            ways[0][0][0] = 1;\n\n            Deque<State> queue = new ArrayDeque<>();\n            queue.offer(new State(0, 0, 0, 0));\n\n            while (!queue.isEmpty()) {\n                State cur = queue.poll();\n                int x = cur.x;\n                int y = cur.y;\n                int side = cur.side;\n                long d = dist[x][y][side];\n\n                if (side == 0) {\n                    int rem50 = cnt50 - x;\n                    int rem100 = cnt100 - y;\n                    for (int take50 = 0; take50 <= rem50; take50++) {\n                        for (int take100 = 0; take100 <= rem100; take100++) {\n                            if (take50 + take100 == 0) continue;\n                            if (take50 * 50 + take100 * 100 > K) break;\n\n                            int nx = x + take50;\n                            int ny = y + take100;\n                            int nside = side ^ 1;\n                            long nd = d + 1;\n\n                            if (dist[nx][ny][nside] >= nd) {\n                                if (dist[nx][ny][nside] > nd) {\n                                    dist[nx][ny][nside] = nd;\n                                    queue.offer(new State(nx, ny, nside, nd));\n                                }\n                                ways[nx][ny][nside] = (ways[nx][ny][nside] + comb(ways[x][y][side], rem50, take50, rem100, take100)) % MOD;\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                } else {\n                    int rem50 = x;\n                    int rem100 = y;\n                    for (int take50 = 0; take50 <= rem50; take50++) {\n                        for (int take100 = 0; take100 <= rem100; take100++) {\n                            if (take50 + take100 == 0) continue;\n                            if (take50 * 50 + take100 * 100 > K) break;\n\n                            int nx = x - take50;\n                            int ny = y - take100;\n                            int nside = side ^ 1;\n                            long nd = d + 1;\n\n                            if (dist[nx][ny][nside] >= nd) {\n                                if (dist[nx][ny][nside] > nd) {\n                                    dist[nx][ny][nside] = nd;\n                                    queue.offer(new State(nx, ny, nside, nd));\n                                }\n                                ways[nx][ny][nside] = (ways[nx][ny][nside] + comb(ways[x][y][side], rem50, take50, rem100, take100)) % MOD;\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n\n            if (dist[cnt50][cnt100][1] == INF) {\n                out.println(-1);\n            } else {\n                out.println(dist[cnt50][cnt100][1]);\n            }\n            out.println(ways[cnt50][cnt100][1]);\n        }\n\n        static class State {\n            int x, y, side;\n            long d;\n            State(int x, int y, int side, long d) {\n                this.x = x;\n                this.y = y;\n                this.side = side;\n                this.d = d;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    static class InputReader {\n        private final InputStream in;\n        private final byte[] buffer = new byte[1024];\n        private int ptr = 0, len = 0;\n\n        InputReader(InputStream in) { this.in = in; }\n\n        private int read() {\n            if (len == -1) throw new RuntimeException();\n            if (ptr >= len) {\n                ptr = 0;\n                try { len = in.read(buffer); } catch (IOException e) { throw new RuntimeException(); }\n                if (len <= 0) return -1;\n            }\n            return buffer[ptr++];\n        }\n\n        public int nextInt() {\n            int c = read();\n            while (isSpace(c)) c = read();\n            int val = 0, sign = 1;\n            if (c == '-') { sign = -1; c = read(); }\n            for (; '0' <= c && c <= '9'; c = read()) val = val * 10 + c - '0';\n            return val * sign;\n        }\n\n        private boolean isSpace(int c) { return c == ' ' || c == '\\n' || c == '\\r' || c == '\\t' || c == -1; }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\nMOD = 1000000007\nINF = 10**18 + 1\n\nclass InputReader:\n    def __init__(self, stream):\n        self.stream = stream\n        self.buffer = b''\n        self.pos = 0\n    \n    def _fill_buffer(self):\n        data = self.stream.read(1024)\n        if not data:\n            return False\n        self.buffer += data\n        return True\n    \n    def _next_byte(self):\n        while self.pos >= len(self.buffer):\n            if not self._fill_buffer():\n                return -1\n        byte = self.buffer[self.pos]\n        self.pos += 1\n        return byte\n    \n    def next_int(self):\n        c = self._next_byte()\n        while c in (32, 10, 13, 9):  # space, newline, carriage return, tab\n            c = self._next_byte()\n        sign = 1\n        if c == 45:  # '-'\n            sign = -1\n            c = self._next_byte()\n        val = 0\n        while 48 <= c <= 57:  # '0' to '9'\n            val = val * 10 + (c - 48)\n            c = self._next_byte()\n        return val * sign\n\ndef precompute_nCr(max_n):\n    nCr = [[0] * (max_n + 1) for _ in range(max_n + 1)]\n    for i in range(max_n + 1):\n        for j in range(i + 1):\n            if j == 0 or j == i:\n                nCr[i][j] = 1\n            else:\n                nCr[i][j] = (nCr[i-1][j] + nCr[i-1][j-1]) % MOD\n    return nCr\n\ndef comb(base, a, b, c, d, nCr):\n    result = (base * nCr[a][b]) % MOD\n    result = (result * nCr[c][d]) % MOD\n    return result\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    idx = 0\n    n = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    K = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    \n    cnt50 = 0\n    cnt100 = 0\n    for _ in range(n):\n        val = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n        if val == 50:\n            cnt50 += 1\n        else:\n            cnt100 += 1\n    \n    # Precompute binomial coefficients\n    nCr = precompute_nCr(99)\n    \n    dist = [[[INF] * 2 for _ in range(200)] for _ in range(200)]\n    ways = [[[0] * 2 for _ in range(200)] for _ in range(200)]\n    \n    dist[0][0][0] = 0\n    ways[0][0][0] = 1\n    \n    queue = deque()\n    queue.append((0, 0, 0, 0))  # x, y, side, d\n    \n    while queue:\n        x, y, side, d = queue.popleft()\n        \n        if side == 0:\n            rem50 = cnt50 - x\n            rem100 = cnt100 - y\n            for take50 in range(rem50 + 1):\n                for take100 in range(rem100 + 1):\n                    if take50 + take100 == 0:\n                        continue\n                    if take50 * 50 + take100 * 100 > K:\n                        break\n                    \n                    nx = x + take50\n                    ny = y + take100\n                    nside = side ^ 1\n                    nd = d + 1\n                    \n                    if dist[nx][ny][nside] >= nd:\n                        if dist[nx][ny][nside] > nd:\n                            dist[nx][ny][nside] = nd\n                            queue.append((nx, ny, nside, nd))\n                        ways[nx][ny][nside] = (ways[nx][ny][nside] + comb(ways[x][y][side], rem50, take50, rem100, take100, nCr)) % MOD\n        else:\n            rem50 = x\n            rem100 = y\n            for take50 in range(rem50 + 1):\n                for take100 in range(rem100 + 1):\n                    if take50 + take100 == 0:\n                        continue\n                    if take50 * 50 + take100 * 100 > K:\n                        break\n                    \n                    nx = x - take50\n                    ny = y - take100\n                    nside = side ^ 1\n                    nd = d + 1\n                    \n                    if dist[nx][ny][nside] >= nd:\n                        if dist[nx][ny][nside] > nd:\n                            dist[nx][ny][nside] = nd\n                            queue.append((nx, ny, nside, nd))\n                        ways[nx][ny][nside] = (ways[nx][ny][nside] + comb(ways[x][y][side], rem50, take50, rem100, take100, nCr)) % MOD\n    \n    if dist[cnt50][cnt100][1] == INF:\n        print(-1)\n    else:\n        print(dist[cnt50][cnt100][1])\n    print(ways[cnt50][cnt100][1])\n\nsolve()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.8053239627042785e-05, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.006769106257706881, -0.0019160023657605052, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -0.0008061258122324944, -0.00011085849109804258, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00016497205069754273, -0.002235058695077896, -0.03414773941040039, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -2.4437606043647975e-05, 0.0, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.17976805567741394, -0.00010930894495686516, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -0.015840059146285057, 0.0, -1.0967194612021558e-05, -1.0609570381348021e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -6.615896563744172e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0002587698982